:: Story promise [guide locked] {"position":"100,550","size":"100,100"}
In a cyberpunk Old Sana'a where clean water is rationed and acid rain makes the streets dangerous, a disgraced covert operative escapes prison with help from a masked cyborg dancer. He wants revenge on the security chief who secretly ordered his parents killed.

Engine: mistaken identity and corrupted trust.
Central question: when institutions control water, information, bodies and truth, can people fight back without becoming another instrument of control?

Title: Neon Glitch (decided 2026-10-26). No calendar year: "the ration era".

[[Rydan]]
[[Characters]]


:: Characters [character guide] {"position":"250,550","size":"100,100"}
Playable: [[Rydan]].
Story cast: [[Bilqis]], [[Zayd]], [[Roya]], [[Numan]], [[Kanan]], [[Bilal]], [[The sheikh]], [[Roya's husband]], [[Rebel robot]].
Retired names: Danzo (now Numan), Karib, Kaid, Rayan, Yazan.

Numan ordered the operation that killed Rydan's parents. Kanan framed Rydan and misled Bilal. Bilal believed the lie and survived. Bilqis helps Rydan escape and hides her own agenda. Zayd reaches prison through a separate corruption case. Roya becomes a rebel after personal and institutional losses.


:: Bilqis [character draft] {"position":"400,550","size":"100,100"}
Cyborg, hacker, dancer under concealment. Cybernetic forearms, facial hardware, cybernetic eyes, turquoise braid, hooded dark outfit with ornate trim. The dancer persona hides who she is; disguise can change clothes, veil, hair, light and behaviour, but the metal stays (hidden plausibly, or leaving tells).
Seems to have impossible powers; really technology, training and a dangerous system whose history is a mystery. Age and past stay mysterious.
Not playable for now.

[[Apparent magic]]
[[Bilqis's signal or payload]]


:: Zayd [character draft] {"position":"550,550","size":"100,100"}
Rookie police officer and Rydan's prison-era ally. Polite, conscientious, inexperienced. Jailed through a police-corruption case separate from Rydan's frame-up. His look is not designed yet.
Note for Claude: code id "zayd" was Rydan until 2026-10-27 (now "rydan", rydan-moves.md); this officer's code id is "officer_zayd".

[[Zayd's first shift]]


:: Roya [character draft] {"position":"700,550","size":"100,100"}
A survivor who becomes a rebel. Mzayyinah by birth; the sheikh's adoption likely gives her lasting status. Her husband dies from delayed injury complications and city exploitation. Not evil; may use ruthless tactics, in uneasy alignment with Bilqis.
Opens the game in a teaser; her full story comes later. A playable Roya segment is possible later, not in the demo.

[[Roya cold open]]
[[Roya's full history]]


:: Numan [character locked] {"position":"850,550","size":"100,100"}
Head of covert operations, security chief. Secretly ordered the operation that killed Rydan's parents. Rydan kills him (boss fight and moral choice). Formal title open.

[[Numan falls]]


:: Kanan [character draft] {"position":"100,700","size":"100,100"}
Rydan's brother; architect of the frame-up. Manipulated secret orders and evidence: made Bilal think Rydan is dangerous, made Rydan think Bilal was dead or a traitor. Wants influence or power; his ego gives away a secret. Fate open.

[[Kanan exposed]]


:: Bilal [character draft] {"position":"250,700","size":"100,100"}
Rydan's covert-ops partner. Rydan did not kill him; he escaped alive. Kanan made him believe Rydan is evil. Returns as a bounty-hunt boss; the truth allows reconciliation.

[[Bilal returns]]


:: The sheikh [character draft] {"position":"400,700","size":"100,100"}
Hears Roya's story at the checkpoint and adopts her, which lets the marriage go ahead. Killed in the gang attack at the wedding; the adoption did not cause his death.


:: Roya's husband [character idea] {"position":"550,700","size":"100,100"}
Roya's beloved and husband, from a tribal family. Badly hurt in the wedding attack; dies later of complications after they struggle in Old Sana'a. Name and background open.


:: Rebel robot [character idea] {"position":"700,700","size":"100,100"}
An advanced, nonconforming robot or cyborg unit near Numan; a possible later ally or complication. Optional until the story needs it.


:: Tayramana [place draft] {"position":"850,700","size":"100,100"}
A refuge room with coloured qamariya light, herbs and qishr: warm and domestic against the hostile street. People shelter here from acid rain.
Could pair with the sabil save spot.


:: Apparent magic [place locked] {"position":"100,850","size":"100,100"}
Nothing is supernatural; every "power" has a biological, chemical, psychological or technological cause, and limits.
- Reading a crowd: observation, records, wearable telemetry, signal analysis. Can be wrong.
- A dancer controlling a room: choreography, light, sound and timed exploits of compatible implants. No control of unmodified minds.
- "Zombies": impaired people plus hijacked prosthetics. No resurrection.
- Hybrid virus: a biological agent plus a digital payload for implants. Origin, scope and cure open.
- Jambiya slots: engineered modules that draw charge, heat up and wear down.

[[Bilqis's signal or payload]]


:: Jambiya hilts [locked] {"position":"250,850","size":"100,100"}
Rydan owns three complete jambiyas, each a hilt plus a blade. Exactly three hilts in the game:
1. Prison escape: 1 slot. He starts with it.
2. After defeating Numan: 2 slots (origin open).
3. Grandfather's grave and restored family house: 3 slots, the heirloom.
Much later: all three chained into one weapon (heavier, harder to control).
Blades vary separately. Slots do not make energy: what goes in draws charge, heats up and wears down.

[[Slot contents]]


:: Roya cold open [scene ch0 draft] {"position":"400,850","size":"100,100"}
Plays after the start flow, before the escape, in normal game graphics (not a Flow video). Acid rain drums on a roof. Through a band of qamariya glass, Roya watches a ration checkpoint: guards, a queue, a delivery cart that should have gone to a clinic. Her face is half hidden; a glimpse of a prosthetic hand or rebel signal. A system alert starts to identify her. She protects someone in the queue and gives away her position. Cut to black.
Open: does the player control Roya here, or only watch?
Claude default 2026-10-26, Feras to confirm: watch only (a playable Roya comes later, not in the demo). Built that way in the first playable (docs/design/first-playable.md).

[[Prison escape]]


:: Prison escape [scene ch1 draft] {"position":"550,850","size":"100,100"}
Playable tutorial. Rydan is held for killing Bilal and bringing a foreign woman in. Power flickers, alarms, coordinated confusion: Bilqis, hidden behind her dancer identity, helps from outside by hitting compatible systems and timing diversions. Rydan fights out with the 1-slot prison jambiya: movement, combat, cover, one tech interaction.
Rookie prisoner Zayd and some inmates get swept up. Rydan knows the layout and lets Zayd think he is leading. Bilqis's help leaves a trace security can follow.

[[Rooftop fight]]
[[Zayd's first shift]]


:: Zayd's first shift [scene ch1 draft] {"position":"700,850","size":"100,100"}
Card: "Earlier". Rookie officer Zayd's first shift in Old Sana'a. A masked gang causes trouble over a contested street or delivery route (motive open; water-corridor extortion is the strong option). Some officers want to let them go, erase evidence or protect a patron. Zayd talks a few into stopping the gang, and makes enemies.
Check later: is this rewind played as Zayd, or shown as scenes? (The bible keeps the playable view on Rydan.)

[[Zayd's corruption case]]


:: Zayd's corruption case [scene ch1 draft] {"position":"850,850","size":"100,100"}
A separate police-corruption case: records altered, a witness pressured or evidence planted to make Zayd look guilty. He is arrested and sent to the prison where Rydan already is. His timeline catches up to the escape.

[[Prison catch-up]]


:: Prison catch-up [scene ch1 draft] {"position":"100,1000","size":"100,100"}
Back to the escape at a clear visual beat (the same alarm light or qamariya reflection), not a replay. Rydan and Zayd's uneasy partnership goes on.

[[Demo end]]


:: Demo end [scene ch1 draft] {"position":"250,1000","size":"100,100"}
A decisive escape and a new objective: reach a contact, expose a security lie, or find a route toward Numan. Tease Bilqis's bigger capability without explaining it. Roya's origin and Numan's death are saved for later.

[[Chapter 2]]


:: Rydan and the frame-up [scene ch2 draft] {"position":"400,1000","size":"100,100"}
Childhood: Numan's covert operation kills Rydan's parents; someone shelters him (maybe Bilqis; keep it restrained). His family may have been tied to an outlawed technical tradition outsiders call witchcraft (open).
Adulthood: he joins covert ops, partners with Bilal. Kanan forges orders and evidence; Rydan is framed for Bilal's "murder" and for bringing Bilqis in.
Told through later flashbacks or evidence. The reveal: he served for years in the institution that destroyed his family.

[[Numan falls]]


:: Numan falls [scene ch2 draft] {"position":"550,1000","size":"100,100"}
Boss fight and moral choice, not just a revenge cutscene. Rydan kills Numan. Emergency rule follows: tighter surveillance, street fighting through the qamariya-lit city. Rydan and Bilqis become the most wanted people, dead-only bounties. Rydan gains the 2-slot hilt.

[[Bilal returns]]


:: Bilal returns [scene ch3 draft] {"position":"700,1000","size":"100,100"}
During the bounty hunt Bilal comes as a boss. He believes Rydan is the traitor who tried to kill him. The fight comes from Kanan's lie, not a villain reveal.

[[Kanan exposed]]


:: Kanan exposed [scene ch3 draft] {"position":"850,1000","size":"100,100"}
A three-way encounter: Rydan, Bilal, Kanan. Provoked, Kanan's pride makes him correct a detail of a forged order that only its forger could know. Rydan and Bilal see the truth and turn on his scheme; they reconcile before his fate is decided.
Fate open: Rydan kills him, Bilal kills him, or he escapes.

